========================================================================
SOURCE REVIEW (7.2 — no product edit)
========================================================================

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo` (240 lines, under monofile ratchet / soft 256):

```
pub fn c_sys_exec_last_arg(args: String) -> String
  if n == 0 → return "oo_str_lit(\"\")"
  linear walk of C arg text
  skip "..." with \\ escapes (in_str)
  paren depth — commas at depth>0 do not split
  top-level ',' → last_start = first non-space after
  if last_start >= n → return args
  out = str_slice(args, last_start, n)   // ONE slice
  if out == "" → return args
  return out
```

Static: **no** `last = last +` / `out = out + c` inside this function.
The only `out = out + c` in the monofile is `c_args_strip_cr` (8.6 CR
filter) — **not** 7.2.

Call site (`c_emit_secret_guard.oo` L130–140):

```
if sink == "sys_exec":
  refuse a1, a2 if present
  last = c_sys_exec_last_arg(args)
  if last != "" && c_arg_is_cap_ident(last):
    c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(env, sink, last)
```

`c_arg_is_cap_ident` rejects `"`, `(`, `)`, space, comma — so a quoted
last span cannot last-arg-refuse. Full `c_guard_scan_idents` also walks
`sys_exec` args (7.1) and skips strings. Dual coverage: last-arg + ident
scan. Check dual: `c_secret_scan_call(..., want=1, eq_only=false)` walks
token IDENTs at argi≥1 (so last IDENT after a cap is in-scope).

Host vs source: `c_emit_args.oo` mtime **07:12** < host **07:49**. Slice
comment/body predates the product binary. Later comment-only edit
(runtime note, file now 240) does **not** change extract semantics.

